    {
      "address": "0x3DCD",
      "comment": "Запуск музыкального трека. HL=данные установки трека @0x3DE8, DE=0x03F8, BC=3; DI; CALL func_memcpy_keep_psw(0x3DB8) копирует 3 байта установки; EI; затем программирует KR580VI53: OUT 08h значениями 0x36/0x76/0xB6 (counter0/1/2, mode 3 прямоугольная волна). Инициализирует 3-канальный генератор тонов для воспроизведения музыки. Вызывается через обёртку 0x388C.",
      "links": [
        "0x3DE8",
        "0x3DB8"
      ],
      "name": "func_music_start_track",
      "properties": {
        "params": "in: none (fixed: setup data @0x3DE8); out: none. Copies 3 setup bytes to 0x03F8 and programs VI53 control words 0x36/0x76/0xB6 to port 08h."
      },
      "size": 26,
      "type": "function"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x3DE8",
      "name": "data_music_track_setup",
      "size": 3,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x3E1A",
      "comment": "Stage11: Title-melody SCORE control block (15 bytes, ROM @0x3E1A). var_music_track_ptr(0x3854)=0x3E1A points here. Layout: +0=0x38 (base byte -> op7/toggle); +1=0x06 = BASE NOTE (semitone offset added to every voice note code); +2=0x06 = DURATION = 6 VBlank ticks per step (tempo); +3=0x0F op8 (gate ch0); +4=0x00 op9 (gate ch1); +5=0x0E op10 (gate ch2); +6/+7/+8 = 0x60(96) per-voice LOOP LENGTH (each stream wraps at 96 steps); +9=0x1F op6; +A=0 op11; +B=3 op12; +C=2 op13; +D=5 = ch0 per-tick modulation (vibrato) row in data_music_vibrato_table; +E=0. NOTE: this engine has NO separate DEFW pointer table; the three voice note-streams are at fixed offsets from var_music_track_base(0x3856)=0x3E29: track01=0x3E29, track02=base+0x100, track03=base+0x200 (func_music_init@0x3D4E seeds stream-base ptrs 0x383F/0x3841/0x3843 with stride +0x100).",
      "links": [
        "0x4029",
        "0x3E29",
        "0x3F29",
        "0x421A"
      ],
      "name": "data_music_scores",
      "size": 15,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x3E29",
      "comment": "Stage11: Voice 01 note stream -> VI53 counter ch0 (port 0Bh). 96 step bytes. Each byte = NOTE CODE: 0x00 = REST (silence, period slot left as rest); else pitch = data_music_period_table[BASE(=scores+1=6) + code]. This voice uses no bit7 commands (all codes <=0x39). Fixed note length = scores+2 = 6 ticks. Per-tick vibrato offset from data_music_vibrato_table (stride 20, row = scores+13). Current read addr = var_music_stream_base_01(0x383F) + var_music_ptr_01(0x383B). Processed by func_music_process_voice @0x39D3.",
      "links": [
        "0x383B"
      ],
      "name": "data_music_track_01",
      "size": 96,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x3F29",
      "comment": "Stage11: Voice 02 note stream -> VI53 counter ch1 (port 0Ah). 96 step bytes. Same format as track_01: 0=REST, else period = data_music_period_table[6 + code]. No bit7 commands. Read addr = var_music_stream_base_02(0x3841) + var_music_ptr_02(0x383C). Processed by func_music_process_voice @0x3A32.",
      "links": [
        "0x383C"
      ],
      "name": "data_music_track_02",
      "size": 96,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x4029",
      "comment": "Stage11: Voice 03 note stream -> VI53 counter ch2 (port 09h, bass). 96 step bytes. 0=REST (buf[10] cleared). Bit7 CLEAR (code<0x80): period = data_music_period_table[6 + code]. Bit7 SET (code>=0x80): EXTENDED note -> func_music_set_note_params uses data_note_param_table_43F9[((code&0x7F)-1)*8] 8-byte block: block[0..1]=literal ch2 period, block[3..7]=envelope/gate/timbre params (buf slots 10..14). Read addr = var_music_stream_base_03(0x3843) + var_music_ptr_03(0x383D). Processed by func_music_process_voice @0x3A95.",
      "links": [
        "0x383D"
      ],
      "name": "data_music_track_03",
      "size": 96,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x421A",
      "comment": "Stage11: 96-word (192-byte) 16-bit little-endian CHROMATIC PERIOD TABLE (8 octaves x 12 semitones). Equal temperament: period[i] = round(3822 / 2^(i/12)). Indexed by (BASE + note_code) for all 3 melody voices in func_music_process_voice. func_snd_calc_period(0x020E) multiplies the value by 12 (DAD sequence = 12x) to form the VI53 counter reload written to ports 0Bh/0Ah/09h. Output frequency = f_VI53 / (12*period), f_VI53 ~ 1.5 MHz (docs/VECTOR_VERIFIED: 1497600..1500000). Reference: i=0 ->3822 ->~32.7Hz = C1 = MIDI 24, so MIDI note = i + 24 (= note_code + BASE + 24 = note_code + 30). i=24 ->956; i=36 ->478 ->~261.5Hz=C4=MIDI60; i=61 ->113 ->~1106Hz. Verified live: buf periods ch0=113=i61, ch1=179=i53, ch2=1073=i22.",
      "name": "data_music_period_table",
      "size": 192,
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x42F9",
      "comment": "Таблица частот/параметров нот для музыкального канала 1, шаг 10 байт на ноту. Индексируется селектором ноты в func_music_play_note_ch1(0x3C7D).",
      "name": "data_note_table_ch1",
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x43F9",
      "comment": "Stage11: data_note_param_table_43F9 — 8-byte-per-entry extended-note parameter table for ch2 (voice 03) when a note code has bit7 SET. Index=((code&0x7F)-1)*8. block[0..1]=literal ch2 period (written to buf[4..5]); block[3..6]->buf[10..13] (gate/envelope/timbre ops 10..13); block[7]!=0 -> set bit5 on op7 toggle buf[14] else clear. Used by func_music_set_note_params(0x3B0F). For MIDI the ch2 pitch of these notes = value in block[0..1].",
      "name": "data_note_param_table_43F9",
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x445D",
      "comment": "Stage11 (renamed from data_note_freq_table_ch0): per-tick pitch-modulation (vibrato) table, 20 bytes per row (stride 0x14). Read by func_music_play_note_ch0(0x3BCA)/ch1(0x3C7D): value = table[ (scores[+13]-1)*20 + tick ] (small 0..3 offsets), ADDED to the channel period in var before OUT, producing subtle vibrato. Row selector = data_music_scores[+0x0D]=5. Inference: amplitude 0..3 on period ~ tens of cents. Not an exact frequency table (period comes from data_music_period_table). Extent unknown (size 0).",
      "name": "data_music_vibrato_table",
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x5000",
      "name": "data_ram_buffer_5000",
      "size": 1024,
      "type": "data"
    },
    {
      "address": "0x6000",
      "comment": "БЛОК ГЛИФОВ (битмапы шрифта), 256 глифов x 32 байта = 8192 байта (0x6000-0x7FFF). Глиф N на 0x6000+N*32. Каждый глиф = 4 цветовые плоскости x 8 байт (8x8 px); plane3 = ~plane0 для рисуемых глифов (4-плоскостная цветовая кодировка); пустой глиф = planes0-2=0x00, plane3=0xFF. Строится при инициализации функцией func_load_glyph_block(0x0401) из упакованных данных шрифта ROM data_packed_font_3041(0x3041). Читается при отрисовке функцией func_render_glyph(0x0803) через data_glyph_ptr_table(0x0600). Это распакованный набор глифов, требуемый TZ Stage 7 шаг 5; база блока = 0x6000 (адрес, относительно которого вычисляются смещения глифов). RUNTIME-VERIFIED: глиф 65 'A' @0x6820 = [00,CC,CC,FC,CC,CC,78,30] x3 плоскости + [FF,33,33,03,33,33,87,CF]; глиф 247 KOI8-R 'В' @0x7EE0 = [00,FC,C6,C6,FC,CC,CC,F8]x3 + инверсия; глиф 155 (блочный символ 0x9B) @0x7360 нарисован; глиф 0 @0x6000 = [00 x24, FF x8]. Тест регенерации: обнуление глифа 65 с последующим запуском func_load_glyph_block(0x0401) восстанавливает корректный битмап 'A' -> подтверждает, что этот ритуал строит блок.",
      "name": "data_glyph_block",
      "size": 8192,
      "type": "data"
    },
